1. COUNT LADDERS AND THE DUODECIMAL GATE
   n  U(n)  Burnside  rooted P(n)  extension E(n->n+1)  self-converse
   1     1         1            1                     2              1
   2     1         1            2                     4              1
   3     2         2            4                    12              2
   4     4         4           12                    48              2
   5    12        12           48                   296              8
   6    56        56          296                                   12

   Duodecimal coincidences:
     P(4) = 12 = 1 dozen rooted/node perspectives on 4-classes.
     U(5) = 12 = 1 dozen unrooted 5-tournament classes.
     SC(6) = 12 = 1 dozen self-converse 6-classes.
     K_{4,5} rectangle redundancy = 4*(4-1) = 12.

   Literal arithmetic check and corrected ledgers:
     48 + 12 = 60, not 56.
     U(6) = P(5) + 8 = 48 + 8 = 56.
     U(6) = P(5) + SC(6) - U(4) = 48 + 12 - 4 = 56.
     defect/U(6) = 1/7; P(5)/U(6) = 6/7.
     defect/dozen = 2/3; overlap/dozen = U(4)/12 = 1/3.
     U(6)/dozen = 14/3; P(5)/dozen = 4.

