5. OBSERVER-EXTENSION / CUT PAYLOAD ABSTRACT
   HYP-3057 value-origin ledger:
     quotient=small integer reused across adjacent levels
     payload=value_origin_type plus the coordinate it came from
     rule=type the number before using it as an invariant
   HYP-3056 observer-cut orbit ledger:
     quotient=visible-fiber automorphism quotient
     payload=orbit of boundary slice / incidence word / extended shadow
     rule=normalize payloads only modulo visible automorphisms
   HYP-3039 controlled forgetting:
     quotient=coarse quotient fiber
     payload=hidden coordinate stage / residual debt
     rule=retain, reconstruct, dual-annihilate, descend, or name debt
   HYP-3038 q=23 drop/add square:
     quotient=fixed-margin rectangle
     payload=exact-M zeta and endpoint-owner strip
     rule=rectangle residue is payload, not count noise
   HYP-3037 residual capacitors:
     quotient=two-plate route cut
     payload=first-cut stage / capacitor id
     rule=cut payload schedules route separation
   HYP-3041 AP-tail repair:
     quotient=AP-core one-tail observer
     payload=q=13 puncture or reciprocal fixed-point clock
     rule=coarse owner strip is unsafe without hidden clock
   HYP-3045 endpoint-owner transfer:
     quotient=B18Z6 endpoint shadow
     payload=external owner strip and transfer delta
     rule=owner names are the extension payload
   HYP-3021/HYP-3022 pair-good decoys:
     quotient=blocker generator quotient
     payload=barcode / normal-fan active owner
     rule=generator class beats raw decoy count
   HYP-3049 ordered-pair sectors:
     quotient=old-root/new-observer cut
     payload=cross-sector orientation word
     rule=first compact sidecar after rooted cache
   HYP-3053 diagonal flow:
     quotient=K_{k,k+1} line quotient
     payload=rectangle/hourglass cycle residue
     rule=redundancy law is the proof carrier
   Abstract law: observer-extension creates a cut payload; controlled
   forgetting may quotient the observer only when that payload is typed
   by origin, reduced to its visible payload orbit, fiber-constant,
   reconstructible, killed by a dual/cycle equation, descended
   familywise, or emitted as named residual debt.

6. TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS
   Vertices are proof carriers, not runners or arcs.
   Pairwise observable: retained LRC predicate payload minus quotient loss.
   Switch: orient toward the carrier that explains an actual lost coordinate;
   ties follow the displayed Hamiltonian path.
   path=exact_canonical_audit > burnside_odd_cycle_sidecar > cross_sector_orientation_word > deletion_parent_fiber_profile > rectangle_hourglass_cycle_residue > self_converse_branch_locus > duodecimal_overlap_ledger > rooted_perspective_cache > raw_orbit_count_coincidence
